Subject: A plain object freed from the zero-count list takes a direct path, and an arena block is freed with one header read

What this does
  - `free_zero_refcount` sends an object with `class_id == JS_CLASS_OBJECT` and no `first_weak_ref` to the new `free_plain_object` instead of
    `free_gc_object` -> `free_object`. It runs the same field loop, prop-array free, shape release, `remove_gc_object` and block free, in the same
    order, and omits the `free_mark` store, the finalizer-table lookup, the `shape`/`prop`/`class_id`/`u` fail-safe stores and the
    REMOVE_CYCLES test.
  - `js_free_rt` frees an arena block from a single read of its header (size class, accounted size, arena, free-list push), instead of
    `js_arena_usable_size` followed by `js_arena_free` re-deriving the same things. Large and zero-size blocks, and the
    `JS_ARENA_LARGE_BLOCKS_ONLY` builds, take the old path. The empty-arena handling moves into the shared `js_arena_empty`.

Why we need it
  The commonest garbage is a plain object. Its free ran through four layers (type switch, class-generic `free_object`, `js_free_rt`,
  `js_arena_usable_size`, `js_arena_free`) that re-test things a plain object cannot have (a finalizer, exotic state, a cycle-collector phase).

Soundness
  free_plain_object is entered only from free_zero_refcount, which sets gc_phase = DECREF for the whole loop and is the only caller of
  free_gc_object besides gc_free_cycles (which runs in REMOVE_CYCLES and is untouched). In DECREF, free_object's last branch is always
  `js_free_rt(p)`, so the zombie re-queue is unreachable here. Dropped stores: free_mark is read only by JS_IsLiveObject and the cycle
  walk of the finalizer-visible zombies, both reachable only for objects that outlive free_object (REMOVE_CYCLES); shape/prop/class_id/u are
  dead stores into a block released at the end of the same call, and no code runs between them and the release for a class without a
  finalizer (reset_weak_ref is excluded by the first_weak_ref test). rt->class_array[JS_CLASS_OBJECT].finalizer is NULL by construction
  (the class table entry is {Object, NULL, NULL} and JS_NewClass refuses an id already registered); asserted. Child values released in the field
  loop go through js_free_value_rt, which in DECREF only moves them onto the zero list (no nesting), exactly as before. js_free_rt's
  fused path computes the same free_size (block_size - header + MALLOC_OVERHEAD), the same underflow check before any mutation, the same
  counters and the same free-list/arena transitions as usable_size + js_arena_free; js_arena_empty is the old tail verbatim. Accounting
  (malloc_count/malloc_size, JS_ComputeMemoryUsage) is unchanged: verified equal on the interpreter shell.

Functions touched
  `free_zero_refcount`, `free_plain_object` (new), `js_free_rt`, `js_arena_empty` (new, split out of `js_arena_free`), `js_arena_free`

No.

